1. OpenColorIO, ACES 2.0 output transform
   Source: https://github.com/AcademySoftwareFoundation/OpenColorIO
           src/OpenColorIO/ops/fixedfunction/ACES2 (Common.h, ColorLib.h, MatrixLib.h, Transform.cpp)
           and the renderer in FixedFunctionOpCPU.cpp, at commit 22dd9c4faa
   Copyright Contributors to the OpenColorIO Project.
   License: BSD 3-Clause, LICENSES/OpenColorIO-BSD-3-Clause.txt
   Changes: translated from C++ to Swift in Modules/VLProcessing/ACES2.swift, keeping only the
   forward path, with the built-in Rec.709 and P3-D65 1000-nit views' clamps and display
   encoding from transforms/builtins/ACES.cpp and Displays.cpp added in
   Modules/VLProcessing/BuiltInLook.swift.

2. OpenColorIO, ACES 1.x SDR video output transform
   Source: https://github.com/AcademySoftwareFoundation/OpenColorIO at commit 22dd9c4faa:
           "ACES-OUTPUT - ACES2065-1_to_CIE-XYZ-D65 - SDR-VIDEO_1.0" in
           src/OpenColorIO/transforms/builtins/ACES.cpp, the ACES glow, red modifier and
           dark-to-dim renderers in ops/fixedfunction/FixedFunctionOpCPU.cpp, the curve fitting in
           ops/gradingrgbcurve/GradingBSplineCurve.cpp, and the Rec.1886 Rec.709 display in
           transforms/builtins/Displays.cpp
   Copyright Contributors to the OpenColorIO Project.
   License: BSD 3-Clause, LICENSES/OpenColorIO-BSD-3-Clause.txt
   Changes: translated from C++ to Swift in Modules/VLProcessing/ACES13.swift, keeping only the
   forward path of that view, clamped to the display.

3. OpenColorIO Configuration for ACES, camera input matrices
   Source: https://github.com/AcademySoftwareFoundation/OpenColorIO-Config-ACES, the ACES 2.0 and
           1.3 studio configs, as built into OpenColorIO 2.6
   Copyright Contributors to the OpenColorIO Project.
